## Changes

### 1. `crates/ruff_linter/src/rules/pyflakes/rules/strings.rs`
Extended `percent_format_positional_count_mismatch` (F507) with a new branch. Previously, when the RHS type was `Unknown` (variables, calls, attribute accesses, subscripts), the rule never fired because such values could be tuples at runtime. Now, when the format string has **zero** placeholders, these are flagged — because the *only* valid substitution for a zero-placeholder format string is the empty tuple `()`, which is already handled by the `Expr::Tuple` branch (`found == 0 == num_positional`). Everything else is guaranteed to raise `TypeError` at runtime.

```rust
} else if summary.num_positional == 0 {
    // The RHS has an unknown type (a variable, call, attribute access,
    // etc.). It could be a tuple at runtime, so it can only be a valid
    // substitution for a format string with zero placeholders if it is the
    // empty tuple `()` — which is handled by the `Expr::Tuple` branch
    // above. Any other non-empty right-hand side is a single substitution
    // that will raise at runtime.
    checker.report_diagnostic(
        PercentFormatPositionalCountMismatch { wanted: summary.num_positional, got: 1 },
        location,
    );
}
```

Behavior preserved: multi-placeholder format strings with `Unknown` RHS (e.g. `'%s %s' % banana`) still aren't flagged, since the variable could be a tuple of matching arity.

